WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.835
Introducing RackOps Lab.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:13.781
One calm view of your entire lab. Health, incidents, acceptance, and spares, all computed from real records.

3
00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:20.138
When a service fails, it's detected in seconds, and you see exactly where.

4
00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:27.095
Every piece of evidence is captured, timestamped, and kept separate from the diagnosis.

5
00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:35.991
And recovery isn't a button. A wrong fix fails verification. Only proven recovery resolves the incident.

6
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:47.194
New servers are measured against their build sheet. Mismatches fail. Corrections are recorded. And every re-test becomes a new, permanent record.

7
00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:53.618
Explore every rack, and trace any cable, end to end, through every patch panel.

8
00:00:54.867 --> 00:01:00.933
Reserve the right spare, record the swap, and return the failed part, with a complete audit trail.

9
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:07.335
RackOps Lab. Every number labeled. Every action accounted for.
